-- Passage wg9-informative-writing-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('5834fe95-45b3-52fd-9fe4-f9ef8f1c1b6c', 'wg9-informative-writing-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-informative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Bike Sharing Comes to Harlow Point$q$, $q$(1) In 2023, the town of Harlow Point launched a bike-share program. (2) In a bike-share program, a town places public bicycles at docking stations, and riders can unlock a bike with a phone app or a card, ride it, and return it to any station. (3) Harlow Point started with 40 bicycles at eight stations near the library, the train station, the high school and the main shopping street.

(4) Riders pay one dollar to unlock a bike and ten cents for each minute they ride. (5) Students with a school ID ride free on weekdays. (6) Each bike has a basket, lights that turn on automatically and a seat that adjusts without tools.

(7) The program has been more popular than town leaders expected. (8) Some people really like it. (9) Most trips are short, and the most common route connects the train station to the shopping street.

(10) The program has also faced problems. (11) In its first winter, ridership fell sharply because of snow and ice. (12) Several stations also ran out of bikes during busy morning hours while others sat full. (13) To solve this problem, workers now use a van to move bikes from crowded stations to empty ones twice a day.

(14) Harlow Point plans to add four more stations next year, including one at the community pool.$q$, 'draft')
