insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('a0f980fb-185d-59aa-a8ef-4c606fd0c10c', 'wg9-informative-writing-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-informative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$How the Desert Tortoise Survives the Heat$q$, $q$(1) In the Sorrel Valley, summer afternoons regularly reach 45 degrees Celsius, and rain may not fall for months. (2) Few animals could survive there for long, yet the desert tortoise can live for more than fifty years in this harsh place. (3) It survives through a combination of digging, careful timing and water storage.

(4) The tortoise's most important tool is its burrow. (5) Using strong, flattened front legs, a tortoise digs a tunnel that can stretch 2 meters into a hillside. (6) Even when the ground above is scorching, the air deep inside a burrow stays much cooler. (7) A tortoise may spend as much as 95 percent of its life underground.

(8) Tortoises also time their activity carefully. (9) In spring, when wildflowers and grasses are green, they come out in the morning to feed. (10) During the hottest months, they stay in their burrows almost all day and may emerge only after a summer thunderstorm. (11) Tortoises are reptiles, like snakes and lizards.

(12) Finally, a tortoise carries its own water supply. (13) It can store water in its bladder, a sac that normally holds waste, and absorb that water back into its body when it needs it. (14) After a rainstorm, a tortoise may drink enough to equal 40 percent of its body weight.$q$, 'draft')
