  ('b24223b6-a7ef-5528-91a0-8675d30af17e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-narrative-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How does the card described in sentence 15 develop the narrator's point of view?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the narrator now treats the crack as part of the bowl's identity rather than a mistake.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that the narrator wants to hide the crack from the people at the show.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It explains the scientific reason that air bubbles cause clay to crack.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-purpose"},{"text":"It shows that the narrator blames Mr. Adeyemi for the damage to the bowl.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It shows that the narrator now treats the crack as part of the bowl's identity rather than a mistake.$q$, $q$By naming the bowl "with one fault line," the narrator presents the crack openly, which shows acceptance. The card points the crack out, so it cannot mean the narrator is hiding it.$q$, 'draft', '103a1107-a284-5605-bfbd-80966fd173e4')
