  ('59b42f8f-f290-593d-a48d-91a1f4f86572', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-narrative-writing'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 17 to give the story a stronger ending?$q$, $q$[{"text":"On the bus home, I kept staring at the photo, amazed that I had spent all morning searching for something I ended up sitting on.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Rafi found three shell fossils in the first hour, and I found only mud that morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-situation"},{"text":"Pell Creek is about forty minutes from our school, so the bus ride took most of the afternoon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"When we got back to school, we returned the rock hammers and brushes to the supply room.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flat-ending-no-reflection"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$On the bus home, I kept staring at the photo, amazed that I had spent all morning searching for something I ended up sitting on.$q$, $q$The correct choice reflects on the surprise of the discovery and ties back to the narrator's long, empty morning. Returning the tools is an action that does not reflect on the experience.$q$, 'draft', '7df4e7ef-6ff3-5bbd-b157-131f58bd7411')
