values
  ('9529f353-f006-5720-ab7f-8c787cf5b0b5', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g9-narrative-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence after sentence 4 that shows the narrator's attitude toward the job before the discovery. Which sentence does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The historical society keeps its oldest records in a room with a cool, steady temperature.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"},{"text":"By the end of my second week, I was starting to doubt that anything interesting would ever turn up.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Mrs. Halvorsen has worked at the historical society for more than twenty years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"focuses-wrong-character"},{"text":"The ledgers listed what customers bought, such as nails, sugar, and lamp oil.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-without-feeling"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By the end of my second week, I was starting to doubt that anything interesting would ever turn up.$q$, $q$The correct sentence reveals the narrator's boredom, which makes the surprise of the letter stronger. The ledger contents describe the job but show no feeling about it.$q$, 'draft', '6d4f6128-55e8-5a46-a184-6568f6bf4b5c')
