   $q$Read the sentence: "The volunteers, who were from the high school, cleaned the riverbank, and they collected 200 pounds of trash, which was mostly plastic." Which revision is most concise while keeping every fact?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Volunteers cleaned the riverbank and collected 200 pounds of trash.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"loses-detail"},{"text":"High school volunteers cleaned the riverbank and collected 200 pounds of plastic.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-meaning"},{"text":"The volunteers from the high school cleaned the riverbank, and they collected 200 pounds of trash that was mostly plastic.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wordy-phrase"},{"text":"High school volunteers cleaned the riverbank and collected 200 pounds of trash, mostly plastic.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$High school volunteers cleaned the riverbank and collected 200 pounds of trash, mostly plastic.$q$, $q$The correct choice keeps the school, the place, the amount and the type of trash in fewer words. The choice saying "200 pounds of plastic" is shorter but changes the meaning, since the trash was only mostly plastic.$q$, 'draft', null)
