   $q$Read the sentences: "My aunt trained for months. She finished the half marathon. She was the youngest runner in her group." Which choice combines them most clearly and correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"After training for months, my aunt finished the half marathon as the youngest runner in her group.","is_correct":true},{"text":"My aunt, training for months, finished the half marathon. Being the youngest runner in her group.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-created"},{"text":"My aunt trained for months, she finished the half marathon, she was the youngest runner in her group.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"My aunt trained for months and she finished the half marathon and she was the youngest runner in her group.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"stringy-and-chain"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$After training for months, my aunt finished the half marathon as the youngest runner in her group.$q$, $q$The correct choice turns the first and third ideas into an introductory phrase and a prepositional phrase, making one clear sentence. The "and ... and" version is a stringy chain that repeats "she" and does not show how the ideas relate.$q$, 'draft', null)
