   $q$Which sentence about the printing press is correctly punctuated?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The printing press spread ideas quickly; because books became cheaper and more common.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-before-dependent-clause"},{"text":"The printing press spread ideas quickly; books became cheaper and more common.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The printing press spread ideas quickly books became cheaper and more common.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"},{"text":"The printing press spread ideas quickly, books became cheaper and more common.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The printing press spread ideas quickly; books became cheaper and more common.$q$, $q$A semicolon correctly joins two closely related independent clauses. The "; because" version is wrong, because the "because" clause is dependent and cannot follow a semicolon.$q$, 'draft', null)
