   $q$Read the sentences: "Ms. Okafor coaches the debate team. She is a former lawyer." Which choice combines them correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Ms. Okafor coaches the debate team. A former lawyer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-created"},{"text":"Ms. Okafor coaches the debate team, she is a former lawyer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"Ms. Okafor coaches the debate team she is a former lawyer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"},{"text":"Ms. Okafor, a former lawyer, coaches the debate team.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Ms. Okafor, a former lawyer, coaches the debate team.$q$, $q$Turning "She is a former lawyer" into the phrase "a former lawyer" and placing it after the name creates one correct sentence. Joining the two sentences with only a comma creates a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
