   $q$Read the sentence: "The rainforest frogs are tiny, however, their bright colors warn predators to stay away." Which revision is correct?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The rainforest frogs are tiny, however, their bright colors warn predators to stay away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-with-however"},{"text":"The rainforest frogs are tiny however their bright colors warn predators to stay away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"},{"text":"The rainforest frogs are tiny, however; their bright colors warn predators to stay away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaced-semicolon"},{"text":"The rainforest frogs are tiny; however, their bright colors warn predators to stay away.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The rainforest frogs are tiny; however, their bright colors warn predators to stay away.$q$, $q$The semicolon must come before "however," because "however" begins the second independent clause. Placing the semicolon after "however" attaches the word to the wrong clause and leaves a comma splice before it.$q$, 'draft', null)
