   $q$Read the sentences: "The library held a used book sale. The sale raised four hundred dollars. The money will buy new laptops." Which choice combines them most effectively?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The library held a used book sale, it raised four hundred dollars, the money will buy new laptops.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-created"},{"text":"The library's used book sale raised four hundred dollars, which will buy new laptops.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The library held a used book sale. Which raised four hundred dollars to buy new laptops.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fragment-created"},{"text":"The library held a used book sale raising four hundred dollars the money will buy new laptops.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fused-sentence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The library's used book sale raised four hundred dollars, which will buy new laptops.$q$, $q$The correct choice makes the sale the subject and uses a "which" clause for the money's purpose, forming one complete sentence. The version "The library held a used book sale, it raised four hundred dollars, the money will buy new laptops" strings three independent clauses together with only commas.$q$, 'draft', null)
