   $q$Which sentence would best fill the blank in sentence 4 by giving evidence for the idea in sentence 5?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The reading car was painted dark green and had gold letters along each of its sides.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Railroads in the 1920s carried farm goods such as wheat and cattle to cities in the east.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"general-fact-not-text"},{"text":"According to Kowalczyk, when the car stopped in Pell Creek, more than two hundred people lined up before it opened.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Many people today still enjoy reading library books while they ride on trains.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$According to Kowalczyk, when the car stopped in Pell Creek, more than two hundred people lined up before it opened.$q$, $q$Sentence 5 says families were eager for reading material, and a line of two hundred people waiting for the car proves that eagerness. The paint color is from the article but says nothing about how people felt about the books.$q$, 'draft', '8effa8cb-b877-53d5-b31a-3ceef8d9f4ab')
