   $q$Which sentence would best fill the blank in sentence 12 to conclude the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Every student who loses an audition will always become kinder by the end of the school year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Trumpets are brass instruments that need careful breathing and strong lips to play well.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Mateo's journey from jealousy to support shows that a musician's real strength is helping the whole group sound its best.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Priya wins the first chair audition, and Mateo practices his solo loudly in the hallway for a week.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"summary-not-analysis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Mateo's journey from jealousy to support shows that a musician's real strength is helping the whole group sound its best.$q$, $q$The conclusion should return to the claim in sentence 1 and name the change the evidence shows, from jealousy to support. Retelling the audition and hallway practice only repeats early events without stating what they mean.$q$, 'draft', '4e31bf17-6d41-5668-8cfc-b8508b36c22c')
