   $q$Which sentence should replace sentence 2 so that the draft states a clear claim about Adeyemi's study?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Teachers should show cartoons in every class because students enjoy them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-opinion"},{"text":"Adeyemi's study shows that captions help language learners learn and remember new words.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Adeyemi's article is about students, cartoons and a language called Spanish.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"Spanish is spoken by many millions of people in countries around the world.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Adeyemi's study shows that captions help language learners learn and remember new words.$q$, $q$The evidence in the draft is about captions improving quiz scores and memory, so the claim should say that. The choice listing students, cartoons and Spanish only names a topic and makes no point.$q$, 'draft', '11a69fea-2e57-5b33-a9bd-ba786f7c0aed')
