   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence (13) to give the essay a conclusion with a formal style?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Anyone who disagrees has obviously never listened to a really good interview.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dismissive-tone"},{"text":"The department should also take every sophomore on a field trip to the state capital.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"In conclusion, history is a very interesting subject that everyone should study.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"Because oral history builds real research skills without weakening writing, the department should adopt it this spring.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because oral history builds real research skills without weakening writing, the department should adopt it this spring.$q$, $q$The correct choice restates the claim formally and connects it to the evidence about research skills and writing scores. The choice "Anyone who disagrees has obviously never listened to a really good interview" keeps an unfair, dismissive tone toward those who disagree.$q$, 'draft', '78f1f424-df33-5f4d-ae2b-9e30d8b747a8')
