insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('b5feffd2-fb85-56b2-be1b-fa72651b83d9', 'wg10-argument-writing-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$A Piano for Eastbrook Station$q$, $q$(1) Each weekday, nearly 6,000 commuters pass through the waiting hall of Eastbrook Station, most of them staring at their phones in silence. (2) The Eastbrook Arts Council should place a public piano in the waiting hall for anyone to play. (3) When the town of Wren Harbor placed a piano in its ferry terminal three years ago, a survey of 500 travelers found that 72 percent said the music made their wait more pleasant. (4) A public piano also gives young musicians, including students who cannot afford practice space, a place to perform for a real audience. (5) Wren Harbor's terminal staff reported that litter in the waiting area decreased after the piano arrived, possibly because travelers began treating the space with more care. (6) My cousin plays the trumpet in her school band.

(7) Some commuters worry that a piano would create noise in a space where people make phone calls or rest. (8) This objection is reasonable, since not everyone wants music during a stressful trip. (9) The council could limit playing hours to the daytime and place the piano at the far end of the hall, away from the quiet seating area. (10) Others fear the instrument would be damaged. (11) Wren Harbor's piano, which is covered and locked each night, has needed only one repair in three years.

(12) Overall, everybody would love it.$q$, 'draft')
