   $q$Read the sentences: "The new wind turbines spin even in light breezes. The town now buys less electricity from the regional grid." Which choice combines them correctly while showing the relationship between the ideas?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The new wind turbines spin even in light breezes therefore; the town now buys less electricity from the regional grid.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-after-adverb"},{"text":"The new wind turbines spin even in light breezes; therefore, the town now buys less electricity from the regional grid.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The new wind turbines spin even in light breezes, therefore, the town now buys less electricity from the regional grid.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-with-adverb"},{"text":"The new wind turbines spin even in light breezes; therefore the town, now buys less electricity from the regional grid.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-misplaced"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The new wind turbines spin even in light breezes; therefore, the town now buys less electricity from the regional grid.$q$, $q$"Therefore" is a conjunctive adverb, so the semicolon goes before it and a comma follows it. Commas on both sides of "therefore" leave two independent clauses joined only by a comma, which is a comma splice.$q$, 'draft', null)
