   $q$Which sentence about a debate tournament uses a colon correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The judges at the debate tournament were: Ms. Achebe, Mr. Lindqvist, and Dr. Ruiz.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-after-linking-verb"},{"text":"Three judges: scored the final round of the debate tournament, Ms. Achebe, Mr. Lindqvist, and Dr. Ruiz.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-splits-subject-verb"},{"text":"Three judges scored the final round of the debate tournament: Ms. Achebe, Mr. Lindqvist, and Dr. Ruiz.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The judges at the debate tournament included: Ms. Achebe, Mr. Lindqvist, and Dr. Ruiz.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-after-verb"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Three judges scored the final round of the debate tournament: Ms. Achebe, Mr. Lindqvist, and Dr. Ruiz.$q$, $q$"Three judges scored the final round of the debate tournament" is a complete clause, so the colon properly introduces the names. A colon after "were" or "included" splits a verb from its complement or object.$q$, 'draft', null)
