   $q$A student wrote: "The drama club budget covers: costumes, props, and lighting gels." The student's teacher asked for a version that keeps a colon before the list. Which revision does this correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The budget covers: the following, costumes, props, and lighting gels.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-after-verb"},{"text":"The budget covers three kinds of supplies: costumes, props, and lighting gels.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The budget: covers costumes, props, and lighting gels.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-splits-subject-verb"},{"text":"The budget covers; costumes, props: and lighting gels.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-for-colon"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The budget covers three kinds of supplies: costumes, props, and lighting gels.$q$, $q$Adding the object "three kinds of supplies" completes the clause before the colon, so the colon can now introduce the list. "The budget covers: the following, costumes, props, and lighting gels" still places the colon directly after the verb "covers."$q$, 'draft', null)
