   $q$Read the sentence: "___ is the hardest part of training for the triathlon." Which choice correctly completes the sentence with a phrase that can act as the subject?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To swimming in open water","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-verb-form"},{"text":"Swimming in open water","is_correct":true},{"text":"Swims in open water","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"finite-verb-as-subject"},{"text":"Swim in open water","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"base-verb-as-subject"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Swimming in open water$q$, $q$"Swimming in open water" is a gerund phrase, which works as a noun and can serve as the subject of "is." "Swim in open water" is a command form and cannot act as a subject.$q$, 'draft', null)
