  ('b6449363-7c6c-59ba-8374-669b0e6a8a24', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-grammar-usage'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentence: "The town council, which meets on the first Tuesday of each month, approved plans for a new skate park." What kind of clause is "which meets on the first Tuesday of each month"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"a relative clause","is_correct":true},{"text":"an independent clause","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-subordinator"},{"text":"a noun clause","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-relative-noun-clause"},{"text":"an adverbial clause","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-relative-adverbial-clause"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$a relative clause$q$, $q$The clause begins with the relative pronoun "which" and describes the noun "council," so it is a relative (adjective) clause. It cannot stand alone as a sentence, so it is not independent.$q$, 'draft', null)
