   $q$Read the sentence: "The survey results showed ___." Which choice correctly completes the sentence with a noun clause?$q$, $q$[{"text":"that most students walking or biking to school","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"clause-missing-verb"},{"text":"which most students walk or bike to school","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"relative-for-noun-clause"},{"text":"that most students walk or bike to school","is_correct":true},{"text":"because most students walk or bike to school","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adverbial-for-noun-clause"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$that most students walk or bike to school$q$, $q$"Showed" needs an object, and "that most students walk or bike to school" is a complete noun clause that tells what the results showed. The "because" clause is adverbial, so it leaves "showed" without an object.$q$, 'draft', null)
