   $q$How does sentence 16 help the reader experience the end of the race?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It summarizes the whole sprint in a single general statement.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-pacing-speed"},{"text":"It uses dialogue to show how the crew reacted to winning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"no-dialogue-present"},{"text":"It traces the boat's progress step by step, so the reader feels the gap closing.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shifts to the Eastgate coxswain's point of view.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"false-pov-shift"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It traces the boat's progress step by step, so the reader feels the gap closing.$q$, $q$The pattern "past their stern, then their middle seats, then their coxswain" lets the reader watch the boat creep forward. It is not a summary, and no one speaks in the sentence.$q$, 'draft', 'dbd6c007-11e3-54fb-9342-d92d27ecfcd6')
