   $q$Why are the details in sentences 16 and 17 arranged in this order?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They list what the club saw in the order they searched the farmer's fence.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-setting"},{"text":"They follow the balloon's climb, building from the field to the curve of the Earth as the story's high point.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They jump back in time to show the launch from Mr. Petrosyan's point of view.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"false-pov-shift"},{"text":"They move from the most important image to the least important one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-order"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They follow the balloon's climb, building from the field to the curve of the Earth as the story's high point.$q$, $q$The sequence "at first... next... then... finally" mirrors the balloon rising higher, so the story ends on its most striking image. The order builds toward the most important image rather than away from it.$q$, 'draft', '3f8fbc93-449a-5ba5-a6bc-c9f7b410a891')
