  ('9a12cf52-c397-5cd7-9209-992dd1d4dbc3', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g10-narrative-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$How do sentences 13 and 14 develop the narrative?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They add outside pressure that makes the narrator's choice in sentence 16 harder.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They end the conflict between Lola and the pharmacist.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-resolution"},{"text":"They describe the pharmacy's shelves to establish the setting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-setting-with-conflict"},{"text":"They introduce the man in the work jacket as the main character.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-focus"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They add outside pressure that makes the narrator's choice in sentence 16 harder.$q$, $q$The growing line and the loud sigh embarrass the narrator, which raises the stakes of choosing to help Lola instead of rushing her. The man is a minor figure, not the main character.$q$, 'draft', 'e040d615-d767-52eb-8ea7-9c51c889af55')
